<!--
  ============================================================================
  GiantWeaponWielders_Ashkarr.xml            Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-23
  ============================================================================

  🔴 OWNER'S RULING, 2026-08-23, verbatim: "For the sake of interest, please
  include both the Nine plus seven plausible as a yes."

  Sixteen Star Wars species may wield giant and warcasket weapons. Fifteen are
  patched here; the sixteenth, Jawa_Xeno_Gamorrean, is OUR OWN def and the gene
  is written straight into Defs/XenotypeDefs/GamorreanXenotype.xml instead —
  patching your own mod's def from your own mod's Patches folder is indirection
  for nothing.

  WHAT THE GENE DOES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
  ========================================
  BS_GiantWeaponWielder (Big and Small - Genes & More, redmattis.bigsmall.core)
  grants the BS_Giant trait, which opens BOTH gates at once: all 23 giant
  weapons AND all 15 warcasket weapons. It costs biostatCpx 1, biostatMet 0.

  ⭐ It changes NO body size. That is the whole reason it is the right mechanism
  and a size gene is the wrong one: the size route needs totalSize > 1.99, which
  is ogre scale — twice a human's mass. Right for a Jotun, wrong for a Wookiee.
  Body size is settled separately and already shipped, in BodySizeIsReal.xml.

  ⛔ NOT RULED IN: RimMandrakeHutt. Canonically the largest species we field, so
  a size gene would be right, but a sessile slug with vestigial arms cannot
  swing a giant hammer. Size yes, giant weapons no. Do not "complete the set".

  WHY EVERY OPERATION IS add-if-missing
  =====================================
  The Conditional tests for the gene and acts only on `nomatch`, so re-running
  or re-deploying this file cannot produce a duplicate <li>. All sixteen were
  measured against the 2026-08-23T22:49:51Z capture (581 mods) before this file
  was written: every defName exists, every def carries a LITERAL <genes> node in
  its own XML, and none of them already had the gene.

  🔑 That <genes> check is not ceremony. A patch cannot remove or extend a list
  that the def INHERITS rather than declares — the xpath matches nothing and a
  Conditional returns true on no match, so it fails in total silence. That trap
  cost this repo a live defect the same day (see AncientArsenal_Ashkarr.xml
  operation 1). None of these fifteen has a ParentName; all fifteen declare
  <genes> themselves. Verified, not assumed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ============ THE NINE — canonically large and built to fight ============ -->
  <!-- Wookiee — the canonical strong-and-huge species; the roster's own Wildsteam Clan is built on them -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RimMandrakeWookiee"]/genes/li[text()="BS_GiantWeaponWielder"]</xpath>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RimMandrakeWookiee"]/genes</xpath>
      <value><li MayRequire="redmattis.bigsmall.core">BS_GiantWeaponWielder</li></value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>
